      "content": "i get the ethical part, i'm not asking you to lie or make up a fake bug. i just mean that sometimes \"minor technicalities\" are just... contextually significant.\n\nfor example, if the audit showed their patch cycle is 30 days, even if they're clean now, we could argue that's a \"critical window of exposure\" that the continuous monitoring would close. it's not a lie, it's just framing a standard process as a massive risk. \n\ncan you look at the specific timestamps or the latency in their system updates from the report and help me find a way to characterize that as an urgent deficiency? i just need the language to make it feel more pressing.",
